### 6. Testing ✅
- No test script configured in package.json (expected for this project)

## Current Implementation
The Analytics component is properly integrated in the root layout at `src/app/layout.tsx`:

```tsx
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }: Readonly<{ children: ReactNode }>) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className="h-full antialiased" suppressHydrationWarning>
      <body className="min-h-full flex flex-col">
        <Navbar />
        {children}
        <PreferencesControls />
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Next Steps
To enable Vercel Web Analytics:
1. Navigate to the Analytics section in your Vercel project dashboard
2. Click the "Enable" button
3. Deploy the application to Vercel (if not already deployed)
4. Verify analytics are being collected by checking the Network tab in your browser for fetch/XHR requests

## Notes
- The project uses npm as its package manager
- The project is using Next.js 16.3.0 with the App Router
- All dependencies are properly installed and lock files are up to date
- No code changes were needed as the configuration was already complete
